{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/165679-synergy-loss","id":165679,"title":"Synergy loss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-10T23:45:47-07:00","id":165679,"title":"Synergy loss","content":"In my chronicle I don't use humanity, integrity, or whatever the respective trait is. I have always used the option laid out in Mirrors that just scraps it and gives suggestions for traits/rolls for each game line. However, I do know that a geist can come back when they die by losing a point of synergy (unless I've been misinformed, I'm currently reading up on it).<br /> <br /> I will soon have my first geist in a chronicle and Mirrors gives no suggestion for what else to do in that situation.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't run a particularly deadly game, so please don't get that idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just like to be prepared for everything, should a situation arise.<br /> <br /> So, firstly I guess, is this correct? Can a geist &quot;come back&quot; by losing synergy?<br /> And if so, what should I do instead, since we don't use synergy?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T03:11:41-07:00","id":165761,"title":"","content":"When a Sin-Eater dies, their geist resurrects them by pushing the death on to the closest human. This does result in an automatic loss of Synergy, and a reduction of how high their Synergy can go - putting an effective maximum on how many times they can come back. Even if you don't like the morality traits, I'm not sure that scrapping Synergy (or some modified version of it) is a good idea for Sin-Eaters. What the trait represents is how well in sync the host and the geist are, which is an important dynamic with these kind of beings. I'm not certain if the loss of Synergy in resurrection is explained precisely, but it could be understood as their relationship becoming frayed because of the difficulty in bringing the host back again, or it could be the geist taking over more of the connection. Given the dynamic of the &quot;broken&quot;, the human soul might be getting shredded to power the resurrection, giving the geist a stronger grasp [they are described, at Synergy 0, as the geist having full control, with the frayed remains of the human psyche weeping in its mind, driving it insane]. It may be possible to represent that dynamic with the traits you are using. If not, other splats (like Promethean) do resurrection as an auto-drop of their supernatural advantage - Psyche, for Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T14:48:35-07:00","id":166244,"title":"","content":"Or you could do what Mortal Remains does for &quot;ghostwalkers&quot; (Sin-Eaters made with Dark Powers); they can resurrect 5 times. That's it. No more, no less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}